WEBVTT

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:11.780
Here's lunch!

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.240
It's the Galaxy Nauts special.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:16.260
This is...

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:19.790
For space food, it's the same as a normal meal.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:23.820
That's because Galaxy Nauts has gravity control.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.080
So everything is just the same as if we were on Earth.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.930
Kind of feels like we're missing out on the full experience...

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:30.750
Yeah...

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:35.950
What, what? Are you saying you don't like my food?

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:38.100
N-No, we'd never say that!

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.530
We really are going to a far planet, are we?

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:44.850
180,000 light years away.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.810
188,000 light years, to be precise.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:51.530
We're flying at the speed of light for 188,000 light years.

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:53.490
It seems so overwhelming.

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:56.950
By the time we get there, we'll all be old and wrinkly.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:58.330
Ew!

00:00:58.330 --> 00:00:59.620
No way...

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.150
It's going to take that long?

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:03.930
Not to worry.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:05.960
We're going by warp.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:07.550
Warp?

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:08.460
I see!

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.880
So they've already invented warp navigation.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:14.750
Whoa, warp, huh?

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:15.820
Wow!

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:17.150
You guys know what that is?

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:19.080
Nope.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:23.350
Warp is indispensable for starship travel.

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:25.420
Warp, huh...

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:27.940
I never thought I'd experience that for real. {YOU TRAVELED THROUGH TIME TENMA WHAT THE HELL WAS THAT THEN}{TAIMU JANPU!}

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:32.750
Warp will begin momentarily.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:34.730
All passengers, please head to your seats.

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:35.190
Who's there?!

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:39.510
Huh?

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:41.460
I'm sure I saw something...

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:42.910
Saw what, though?

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:46.870
We're supposed to be the only ones on this spaceship.

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:49.660
So someone's here who shouldn't be?

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.280
It might not be human.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:55.350
An unidentified creature could be lurking within the spaceship.

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:57.710
Don't say scary things...

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:59.630
We should probably catch it.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:04.860
Right. There's no telling what it'll do to us during the warp.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:09.970
It's possible that inhabitants from other planets have come to sabotage us.

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:11.460
No way...

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:14.730
Their planet's fate is at stake.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.510
We should anticipate it.

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:18.480
Okay then.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:26.700
Over there!

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:30.350
Really? I didn't see anything.

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:32.530
It was around that door.

00:04:32.530 --> 00:04:33.680
Let's go.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:34.870
Wait!

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:37.570
They could be vicious.

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:39.110
Go with caution.

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:39.950
Okay.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:59.370
This is...

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.370
Something's been eating and leaving a mess.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:04.480
There <i>is</i>  something here.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:05.840
Maybe a space rat?

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:12.830
We can't deny the possibility of a rat that has supersized itself to adapt to zero gravity. {what are u on manabe}

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:19.920
No, no, no!

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.710
Anything but that!

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:25.400
In any case, something is definitely hiding here.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:26.220
Yeah.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:29.110
All that's left to investigate is the dining car.

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:30.300
Wait!

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.970
I have to prepare myself.

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:36.060
Okay.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.330
Bring it on!

00:05:37.330 --> 00:05:38.480
I'm opening the door.

00:05:46.110 --> 00:05:47.420
Shinsuke!

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:48.820
Why are you here?

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.370
You snuck on board?

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:53.860
That's pretty extreme.

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:54.910
I'm sorry...

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:58.440
This person is a teammate of yours, right, Captain?

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:01.550
Oh, I see! I thought you looked familiar!

00:06:01.550 --> 00:06:02.340
So you're from Raimon!

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:04.860
Let me introduce you.

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:06.480
This is Nishizono Shinsuke.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:09.260
He's my friend who's played soccer with me for the longest time.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:11.840
I'm Nishizono Shinsuke.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:14.260
I'm sorry for stirring up trouble.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:16.770
Coach...

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:20.660
Please let Shinsuke come with us!

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:21.440
Please!

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:25.040
I'll do anything, just please let me come!

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:27.320
Coach, I ask for him too!

00:06:31.060 --> 00:06:34.550
You're willing to take on any position I ask of you?

00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:35.580
Y-Yes!

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:39.200
Very well then. You are allowed to come.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.110
All right!

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:42.880
Thank you!

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:45.350
This is great, Shinsuke!

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:46.330
Yeah!

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.280
It's good to be here!

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.180
I like you!

00:06:55.860 --> 00:07:01.130
You came on board to risk your life for your friends, despite having no idea where you were headed.

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:02.520
That makes you a man.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:04.680
I'm Tetsukado Shin.

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:05.640
Nice to meet you.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:06.900
Same here!

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:08.860
Ow, ow, ow!

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:12.040
Sorry! I squeezed too hard.

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:15.330
You have a strong grip. As expected from a boxer.

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:16.830
You know about me?

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:21.580
Yeah, I know the backgrounds of all of Inazuma Japan's members.

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:28.800
Guys like him irritate me the most.

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:31.080
Are you sure about this?

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:34.150
He is not one of the qualifiers you have chosen.

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:36.420
His actions were within my expectations.

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:40.140
So you were testing him then?

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:44.170
<i>No. You will not be of any help.</i>

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:50.940
Nishizono Shinsuke is just as much a necessity for the team as the twelve that are currently here.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:55.170
So he has the beast power as well?

00:07:57.530 --> 00:07:59.500
We will now be warping.

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:03.960
Counting down T minus 20 seconds to warp.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:07.370
If we're warping to get there, it must be a pretty far-off place!

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:09.060
This is kind of exciting!

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:09.670
Yeah!

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:14.430
Soccer on other planets, huh...

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:18.200
Everyone, we should watch out for spaceship sickness.

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:19.570
We'll get spaceship sickness?

00:08:19.570 --> 00:08:21.310
It's very possible.

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:33.460
Warping.

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:57.480
Warp has ended.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:59.660
Normal airspace has been restored.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:02.180
No more...

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:08.770
We have arrived at the planet Sandorias, galaxy coordinates 5867-3071.

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:12.460
So this is a planet outside our solar system...

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:16.060
I see you have arrived safely.

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:17.110
Ozrock!

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:20.020
The sand planet, Sandorias.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:24.120
They will be your first opponent for Grand Celesta Galaxy.

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:29.000
We will now be landing in Sandorias.

00:09:32.510 --> 00:09:35.260
We've entered Sandorias's atmosphere!

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:40.260
Strong winds are always blowing in Sandorias, and the ground surface is mainly a desert.

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:49.530
Through evolving in these harsh conditions, the Sandorians have acquired strong bodies and high athletic skill.

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:56.780
They will be an intimidating opponent for you Earthlings.

00:09:57.350 --> 00:10:00.970
We are now entering Sandorias Station.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:10.830
Now, the main tournament for Grand Celesta Galaxy is to begin.

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:20.340
I don't believe I need to repeat this, but the fate of your planet depends on the outcome of this match.

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:22.720
I wish you luck.

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:26.350
The fate of our planet...

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:42.200
Is Earth still winning?

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:43.440
Yes, milady.

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:49.000
They have won the Galaxy Region A-Block's preliminaries and have proceeded onto the main tournament.

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:50.170
I see.

00:10:52.730 --> 00:10:55.210
Here is a video of their final match in the preliminaries.

00:10:56.260 --> 00:11:00.310
My father also believed in that legend...

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:02.530
There is no need for worry.

00:11:02.530 --> 00:11:07.680
We will eliminate those of the blue planet who threaten our future.

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:13.480
That's...

00:11:15.710 --> 00:11:18.440
Minel, I have a request.

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:19.490
Anything.

00:11:20.350 --> 00:11:23.040
Bring that one to me.

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:24.950
But it is an Earthling.

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:27.550
I don't care.

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:29.660
Just bring that one to me.

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:32.080
Yes, milady.

00:11:38.840 --> 00:11:42.130
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:47.110
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:12:00.130 --> 00:12:04.240
I have been ordered by the esteemed Ozrock to act as your guide.

00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:07.450
I am the coordinator Ishigashi Gorham.

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:09.260
It's nice to meet you!

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:14.600
You are allowed to spend your time freely before the match begins.

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:17.460
Why not take a stroll through town until then?

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:18.600
That sounds like fun!

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:20.510
A sand planet, huh?

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:23.440
Allow me to escort you.

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:37.860
Wow!

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:39.600
Here, on the house!

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:44.110
It's delicious!

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:45.160
It sure is!

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:49.660
Water is valuable here in Sandorias, so this is our best welcoming present!

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.370
I see.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:52.750
It's really tasty!

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:53.710
Sure!

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:58.710
Showing hospitality to guests who've traveled from afar is the way of the prideful Sandorians.

00:12:59.240 --> 00:13:03.440
Even if we <i>are</i>  fighting each other for our survival.

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:06.430
Thank you.

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:08.910
But be careful.

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:11.890
Some of us aren't so keen on visitors from Earth.

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:13.890
Okay...

00:13:16.970 --> 00:13:19.980
Was it a good idea to allow them free time?

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:25.710
The match that will decide the fates of Earth and Sandorias is approaching.

00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:31.000
They must learn the weight of the fight that is to come.

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:36.750
It's so cute!

00:13:37.240 --> 00:13:38.660
Yeah, it sure is.

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:39.210
Come here.

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:46.050
How wonderful...

00:13:59.800 --> 00:14:01.040
It's good!

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:03.400
But I wonder what meat it is.

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:04.440
Dunno...

00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:08.660
It can't be...

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:11.490
Maybe we should pretend we didn't see that...

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:16.120
What a magnificent performance.

00:14:16.310 --> 00:14:20.880
Not even the most experienced of dancers can pull off a magnificent somersault as that.

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:28.260
Just as Ozrock said, the inhabitants of this planet have greater athletic skill than we do.

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:29.440
Yes.

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:31.730
Their ability to jump instantaneously is pretty amazing.

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:33.220
Also, this climate...

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:38.350
It will be interesting to see what the stadium is like.

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:43.480
But no matter what the circumstances, we can't afford to lose.

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:47.640
Sandorias's team must be thinking that way as well.

00:14:50.150 --> 00:14:51.530
That was so good!

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:53.820
Huh? Where are the others?

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:57.110
Did we get split up?

00:14:57.110 --> 00:14:59.040
Hey, what's wrong?

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:01.240
Did you see the others?

00:15:01.240 --> 00:15:03.290
Now that you mention it, I don't see them.

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:05.630
Hey, did you guys see Morimura?

00:15:06.310 --> 00:15:09.420
I think she got lost.

00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:12.020
Or it could be the other way around.

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:14.890
We should all group back together.

00:15:15.420 --> 00:15:16.850
I'll go look for them.

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:20.510
Owww...

00:15:20.510 --> 00:15:21.520
I'm sorry.

00:15:21.860 --> 00:15:23.510
Earthlings, are you?

00:15:23.510 --> 00:15:27.530
How nice of you to come all this way from your itty-bitty planet on the edge of the galaxy.

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:29.530
Who are you?

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:37.330
If these guys are representing Earth, then it's no threat to us at all.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:38.510
Say that again?

00:15:38.510 --> 00:15:39.640
What?

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:43.550
You can't judge us until we've had a go first!

00:15:44.550 --> 00:15:45.790
You seem confident.

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:47.880
Wanna see for yourself?

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:49.590
Don't regret it later.

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:51.770
Stop, Tetsukado.

00:15:51.770 --> 00:15:53.620
Save it for the match.

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:54.710
Yeah.

00:15:54.710 --> 00:15:57.240
If you get hurt here, that would be lame.

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:01.140
Fight! Fight!

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:04.460
Looks like we have no choice.

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:06.650
All right then! A soccer battle!

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:19.450
I should call someone for help.

00:16:26.260 --> 00:16:28.820
Whoever scores first wins.

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:29.800
All right.

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:33.260
We'll show you guys how strong we are!

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:36.260
Right back at you.

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:38.720
Calm down, Tetsukado!

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:42.980
Let's score a goal as quickly as we can and end this so we can find the others.

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:45.980
Okay.

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:46.860
Begin!

00:16:49.930 --> 00:16:52.220
Are you the captain?

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:53.490
I'll crush you!

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:54.490
Look out!

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:06.150
He's got a tough head.

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:08.460
If we get hit with that, we're done for.

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:11.750
You need better aim, Karab. {カラブ}

00:17:11.750 --> 00:17:13.170
Sorry about that, Shaula. {シャウラ}

00:17:13.530 --> 00:17:15.180
I won't miss next time.

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:18.180
They were aiming for him on purpose!

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:19.390
Let's go!

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:25.940
Captain!

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:26.900
Okay!

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:27.940
There!

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:32.530
You kicked too hard!

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:34.060
That can't be...

00:17:34.060 --> 00:17:35.820
You put in too much force.

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:38.770
But I didn't, I just did what I always do.

00:17:38.770 --> 00:17:39.820
Tenma!

00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:42.790
The gravity on this planet is weaker than Earth's!

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:44.510
I see.

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:47.750
So that's why it went so far even though I put in the same amount of force.

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:57.220
Tenma!

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:02.220
This is Sandorias's soccer.

00:18:02.570 --> 00:18:05.370
This tournament decides which of us will live or die.

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:07.730
Let's not go making excuses about the stone-cold truth.

00:18:07.930 --> 00:18:08.570
Tenma!

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:09.900
I'm okay!

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:12.150
Go back to the goal, Shinsuke!

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:14.280
O-Okay...

00:18:14.610 --> 00:18:16.650
Resume the match!

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:21.120
Look out!

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:25.830
Kusaka!

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:32.250
You think you can fight us Sandorians with your itty-bitty power?

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:33.500
You're weak, Earthlings!

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:35.760
I have to stop him!

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:37.220
Leave this to me!

00:18:39.000 --> 00:18:39.800
Damn it!

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:41.090
Outta the way!

00:18:42.710 --> 00:18:43.560
Tetsukado!

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:44.600
Shaula!

00:18:45.170 --> 00:18:45.930
Karab!

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:48.100
Yeah, let's do this!

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:55.860
Tenma!

00:19:03.130 --> 00:19:04.660
Not bad.

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:06.240
But it's futile!

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:11.040
Matatagi!

00:19:13.640 --> 00:19:14.880
Tenma!

00:19:16.660 --> 00:19:18.130
Let's not do this anymore, Captain.

00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:19.820
Matatagi.

00:19:20.170 --> 00:19:21.340
Make the goal.

00:19:22.240 --> 00:19:24.850
If you want to end this match, then we have to win.

00:19:26.710 --> 00:19:30.060
If you want to end it that badly, Earthling, then I will.

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:32.600
Not just the match, but your lives!

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:37.360
If we crush you here, Earth's team will have to forfeit the tournament.

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:39.650
That's what you were after!

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:42.910
We will protect our own planet!

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:44.870
Using our own ways!

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:46.260
Let's go!

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:46.870
Yeah!

